\subtree{\title{Hodge Theoretic Approach}
\p{The most modern view of these results is where [Theorem 1.6](001Y) comes from. Indeed, the statment of the theorem follows without much work from showing that the chromatic polynomial of a graph is the characteristic polynomial of the associated graphic matroid... The real work is showing the stronger result which is that the characteristic polynomial of any matroid is log-concave (N.B. June Huh actually proved the result for chromatic polynomials first, it was then extended to all matroids subsequently in the cited joint work). This is the main thrust of Adiprasito, Huh, and Katz's work; [Joshua Wang](https://joshwang.space/) has produced an excellent [exposition](https://people.math.harvard.edu/~jxwang/HodgeTheoryMatroids.pdf) of this work at a fairly accessible level.}

